.\" Generated from crates/writ-tool/src/specs.rs; do not edit.
.TH WRIT\-NAME 1 2026-10-12 "writ 0.1.0" "writ manual"
.SH NAME
writ\-name \- say who a name refers to
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nh
.ad l
\fBwrit name\fR \fB\-i\fR\ \fIDIR\fR [\fB\-\-key\fR\ \fIPATH\fR]... [\fB\-\-expires\fR\ \fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-note\fR\ \fITEXT\fR] [\fB\-q\fR] \fINAME\fR \fISUBJECT\fR
.ad
.hy
.SH DESCRIPTION
Say that, for the identity in DIR, NAME refers to SUBJECT. Names are local: 'me alice' is whoever you call alice, and someone else's alice is a different name. A name can refer to more than one subject. It then works as a group.
.PP
SUBJECT can be:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ1...                   an id
DIR                        an identity directory (its id is used)
\&'writ1... bob laptop'      a name path: whoever bob calls laptop
FILE                       a public key file, or an OpenSSH .pub file
\&'ssh\-ed25519 AAAA...'      an OpenSSH public key
.fi
.RE
.PP
A name for a leaf key must expire within 24 hours, like a grant to one. writ prints the signed statement and adds it to DIR/issued.writ.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fINAME\fR
the name: one word, or a quoted string
.TP
\fISUBJECT\fR
who the name refers to
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-identity\fR \fIDIR\fR
the identity that signs the statement
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fIPATH\fR
secret key file (default: DIR/current.key); give one \-\-key per key when several keys must sign; '\-' means standard input
.TP
\fB\-\-expires\fR \fIWHEN\fR
when the statement expires: a duration such as 30d or 12h, or a date such as 2027\-01\-01 (default: never)
.TP
\fB\-\-note\fR \fITEXT\fR
text to show with the statement; writ does not use it
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
print only the statement
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help; \fB\-h\fR is short, \fB\-\-help\fR is long
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
success; for questions, the answer is yes
.TP
1
the answer is no: the check, verification, proof or name lookup was denied
.TP
2
an error: bad usage, unreadable input, or a failed operation
.SH EXAMPLES
Call an identity alice:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ name \-i me alice writ1qqq... >> bundle.writ
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add an SSH key to the group 'laptops':
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
writ name \-i me laptops ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub >> bundle.writ
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwrit\fR(1), \fBwrit\-grant\fR(1), \fBwrit\-resolve\fR(1)
